<Base title="A letter from Rachel" description="A warm welcome to I Will Bloom: a journal for your own thoughts, at your own pace."><article class="prose"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Our story</nav><p class="eyebrow">A letter from Rachel</p><h1>A little room for what you carry.</h1><figure class="founder-portrait"><img src="/assets/verified/rachel-founder.webp" width="768" height="1344" alt="Rachel, founder of I Will Bloom, smiling outdoors with a cold drink"/><figcaption>Rachel · Founder of I Will Bloom</figcaption></figure><p>Dear friend,</p><p>I created I Will Bloom following my own experience of cancer treatment. Alongside the appointments and practical arrangements, I wanted somewhere for the emotional weight of it all.</p><p>The journal offers that kind of space: somewhere to pause, acknowledge a difficult feeling or notice something small that mattered.</p><figure class="seaside-journal"><img src="/assets/verified/journal-by-the-sea.webp" width="709" height="950" loading="lazy" alt="Rachel holding the open I Will Bloom journal and a pen by the sea"/></figure><h2>You can make these pages your own.</h2><p>Keep them private, or use them to begin a conversation with someone you trust. Write a little, draw, try a colouring page or spend a moment with a short story.</p><p>There is no need to complete every prompt. You can turn a page, leave it for later or return whenever you feel ready.</p><p>My hope is that I Will Bloom feels like quiet company, with gentle structure when you want a starting point.</p><p>With warmth,<br/><strong>Rachel</strong><br/>Founder, I Will Bloom</p><p><a class="btn" href="/journal/">Explore the journal →</a></p><p class="smallnote">Adapted from the founder’s welcome and letter on the existing I Will Bloom website. Final editorial review pending.</p></article></Base>
